4. the t = 6m prefix/endpoint intersection
============================================================================
  Cutoff H = 64^{5m} = 2^{30m} (a factor 2 below 2^{5t+1}).
  The 2^{5m} residues r_u mod 64^{5m} are pairwise distinct, so
  each 5m-letter prefix u has EXACTLY ONE representative below H,
  and it realizes 5m blocks because that depends only on
  x mod 64^{5m}.  It realizes t = 6m blocks exactly when its
  endpoint v_u satisfies v_u mod 64^m in S_m, the depth-m survivor
  set (|S_m| = 2^m).  Both steps verified below.

  m    t=6m   matches    allowance 84m ref. value least match
