6. verdict
============================================================================
  ACCEPTED, all four corrections: 2^89/3^56 = 1.1827129437 (my
  transcription error, 1.182798 was wrong); B_12 = 6 against 168;
  the largest ratio is B_3/42 = 2/42; sums 65/38 and 66/39.
  ACCEPTED, the lambda-deficit form.  The floor is 2rho^{lambda t-B_t}
  up to constants, so lambda t - B_t -> +infinity along one sequence
  suffices and is weaker than my (iii).  Hierarchy corrected.
  CONFIRMED SHARP.  Their comparison family has exactly
  2^{ceil((5t-2)/6)} members below the cutoff, for every t = 3..14,
  rounding included.  So residues 7/15 mod 64 + nesting +
  valuations 3+6i cannot give anything better than 2^{5t/6}: the
  2-adic axis for B_t is CLOSED at exactly my bound.
  CONFIRMED, the t = 6m reformulation.  One representative per
  5m-prefix below H = 64^{5m}, survival iff v_u mod 64^m in S_m,
  and the counts are
    m=1: 2, m=2: 2, m=3: 3, m=4: 0, m=5: 0, m=6: 1, m=8: 1 (from the depth-48 certificate),
  every one far below the allowance 84m.
  NO BOUND OBTAINED, and the obstruction is now explicit: a match
  is decided by bits 30m..36m of 81^{5m} r_u -- the middle window
  of a multiplication, which the 2-adic side (low bits, the prefix)
  and the archimedean side (top bits, the cutoff) jointly leave
  free.  Against 400 random survivor sets per depth the real counts
  are indistinguishable from Poisson(1), so there is no visible
  structure to convert into an upper bound.
  SCOPE.  Restricted two-block positive-integer claim only.

